WEBVTT

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.010
<i>Kagawa Prefecture.</i>

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:24.300
<i>Located on the north side of Shikoku,</i>

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.300
<i>facing the Seto Inland Sea.</i>

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:28.290
<i>Also known as...</i>

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:29.870
<i>Udon Prefecture.</i>

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.100
Boy, do I miss your family's udon.

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.850
Reopen the restaurant!

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.560
I told you...

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.550
I'm not going to run

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:45.960
an udon restaurant.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:57.700
<b>Poco's Udon World</b>

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:18.540
Aww, what?

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:20.450
You oughta take it over.

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:23.250
Didn't your folks teach ya 
the family recipes and such?

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:25.560
Episode 1:   "Bukkake Udon"

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:24.510
No way. I couldn't.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.250
I didn't learn any of that.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:29.330
Sheesh, you're one cold guy.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:31.940
If I hadn't happened to call ya,

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:33.960
you wouldn't have even 
told me you were in town.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:36.000
Yeah, but...

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.130
We just saw each other at my dad's funeral.

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:39.360
So wrong!

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.470
Ya sound so wrong without your accent!

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:44.470
Man, it really sucks.

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:47.040
Everybody who's been to Tokyo once

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:50.100
starts lookin' down on this 
place like it's in the sticks.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.360
Well, Kagawa really is in the sticks.

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:57.690
There's so much open sky here.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:00.820
Ha! Don't make fun of us 
when you're unemployed.

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:02.400
I'm not unemployed!

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.490
I just asked for some time off so 
I could come back here for a while.

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:08.500
<b>Bukkake Udon
Daien</b>

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:07.570
Thanks for the food!

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:10.960
I can drive ya.

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.640
Nah, that's okay.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:14.170
I'm in the mood for a walk.

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:17.700
Ya know, that part of you 
really hasn't changed.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:21.320
Next time, you be the one 
to get in touch, ya hear?

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:22.550
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:31.940
<b>Shinmiya River Bridge</b>

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:34.590
<i>I'm the son of an udon restaurant owner...</i>

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:38.820
<i>Or I was, to be precise.</i>

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:41.280
<i>I never thought that,</i>

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:43.620
<i>at the milestone age of 30,</i>

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.770
<i>I'd be coming back home to an empty house.</i>

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:51.960
<b>Tawara Noodles</b>

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:50.850
Was it always...

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:54.700
this run-down?

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:28.820
Wh-What was that?

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:30.200
A rat?

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.520
Huh?

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:50.930
<b>Wheat</b>

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.460
Wh-Wheat thief!

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:22.030
<i>What the heck? What's with this place?</i>

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:23.210
<i>I can't take it!</i>

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:25.570
<i>It's scary out in the sticks!</i>

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:31.220
<b>Udon</b>

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:39.290
Howdy do?

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:42.800
Ah... The granny from next door.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:44.210
It's good to see you.

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:48.220
You're little Souta-kun from 
Tawara Udon, aren'tcha?

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:51.780
Look how old you've gotten.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:53.340
Still ain't married,

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:55.710
spent all that time bummin' around in Tokyo,

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:59.210
and now yer back here, are ya?

00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:01.260
<i>This sharp-tongued granny...</i>

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.710
<i>Her words still cut like a knife.</i>

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:05.860
Oh, that reminds me.

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:08.520
The little tyke at your house...

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:08.970
Huh?

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:11.960
Is that your secret love child?

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:12.720
Pardon?

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:14.320
No?

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:15.700
Definitely no.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:19.910
Oh, dear. Where'd the little 
thing come from, then?

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:22.360
I just saw the dearie at your restaurant.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.660
I was sure that was the case...

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:33.050
<b>Tawara Noodles</b>

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:46.820
Our restaurant closed down, you know.

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:49.240
<b>Udon</b>

00:06:49.790 --> 00:06:52.360
Do you know how to get home?

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:54.140
You'll catch a cold out here.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:57.820
Oh, don't worry about the wheat. 
I won't tell on you.

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:09.820
<b>Gurgle</b>

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:12.570
<b>Rumble</b>

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.440
<i>Is that a stomach growl?!</i>

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:15.520
All I have is udon, but...

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:17.200
When it's done, do you want some?

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:22.950
Just sit down anywhere.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:25.090
You can watch TV, too, if you want.

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:28.010
<b>Gurgle</b>

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:28.010
<b>Rumble</b>

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:31.450
Oh, yeah. If I put in green 
onions and ginger, will you—

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:33.620
<i>Raw?!</i>

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:36.310
A lost child?

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:40.050
Yeah. Looks like the kid 
wandered into our yard...

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:43.340
That's all? It's probably one 
of the neighborhood kids.

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:45.940
Nothin' to raise a fuss over.

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:49.940
I don't think this one's 
from the neighborhood.

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:51.740
I mean, the kid has no shoes,

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:53.160
is covered in mud,

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:54.950
was really hungry,

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:57.420
and stole some wheat.

00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:00.710
Since when have you been 
the type to poke his nose

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:02.440
into troublesome stuff like that?

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:04.720
I know, but the kid seems 
to have taken to me...

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:09.700
Ow! Ow! Don't pull!

00:08:10.390 --> 00:08:14.270
Just hurry up and take the kid 
to the police! I'm busy here!

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:16.680
Yeah...

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:19.970
I bet your parents are worried sick.

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:22.870
I have to take you to the police.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:25.940
I'll be right back.

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:28.190
Stay here and watch TV, okay?

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:30.330
<i>Dry your eyes.</i>

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:31.940
<i>Your mascara will run.</i>

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:36.870
<i>Far away on the edge of space, in Galaxy M87,</i>

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:40.130
<i>there lived a terrifying alien</i>

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:42.580
<i>bent on invading Earth.</i>

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:46.300
<i>His name is Ipalnemoani Gaogao,</i>

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:50.920
<i>and he is said to be the most 
fearsome alien in the universe.</i>

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:51.420
<b>Lyrics: Shinomaru Nodoka        Composition: Hashimoto Yukari</b>

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:51.420
<b>Gaogao-chan Exercises</b>

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:57.930
<i>He came from the edge of the universe!</i>

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:01.270
<i>Gao gao...</i>

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:10.860
<i>The scar on his back is 
the mark of a champion!</i>

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:12.380
<i>One, two!</i>

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:18.120
Knowing my dad,

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:20.330
I doubt he threw it away.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:23.490
Oh, here it is!

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:25.590
What's that?

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:30.240
Hello?

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:31.870
Hey, Souta?

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:32.630
Sis?

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:35.070
How goes it? Did ya make 
it to the house already?

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:37.060
Yeah, I just got here.

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:39.240
So how's it goin'?

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:41.320
Is the clean-up comin' along?

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:44.370
No, I only just got here, 
so I haven't done anything.

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:49.030
How much time did ya get off from work?

00:09:49.030 --> 00:09:51.170
Eh, however much...

00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:54.400
What the heck? Well, whatever.

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:58.170
When the mourning period ends, 
we need to get rid of the house,

00:09:58.170 --> 00:10:00.330
so keep it up with the cleanin', okay?

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:03.150
Souta?

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:05.000
Are ya listening?

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:05.910
<i>A notebook?</i>

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:07.830
Yeah, I am.

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:10.740
Well, whatever.

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:13.300
Anyway, I'll come by to help soon.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:14.880
At least get a little bit done by then.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:20.460
Wh-What was that?!

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:22.350
Nothing, nothing.

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:23.140
<b>Notes  Part 1</b>

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:26.280
Good grief... Ya always were clumsy.

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:28.140
You're 30 now, ya know.

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:27.800
<i>This is...</i>

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:30.300
You've gotta get your act together!

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:32.400
<b>Udon Recipe 
For every 400g of wheat flour, 23g of salt 
*In the summer, the dough can get too slack, so add more salt. 
In the winter, the dough will get harder, so use less salt. 
Salt    Water 
Spring/Fall 23g  169cc  
Keep salt concentration high. 
Summer 24g 164cc 
Winter 22g 174cc 
While mixing in water, spread 
your hands and mix quickly. 
*Have salt ready.</b>

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:30.300
<i>Dad's...</i>

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:34.270
Hey, are you listening?

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:36.900
Oh, shoot!

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:40.320
Ribbit, ribbit!

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:42.720
What's that? Is somebody else there?

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:45.520
Uh, no. It's nothing.

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:47.290
I've gotta go, okay?

00:10:46.550 --> 00:10:48.250
What the heck?

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:54.380
Ribbit, ribbit!

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:56.340
What are you doing?

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:59.380
Ribbit, ribbit, ribbit!

00:10:58.690 --> 00:11:00.620
Did you drop something down there?

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:10.330
Ow...

00:11:22.150 --> 00:11:23.910
Ribbit, ribbit!

00:11:25.430 --> 00:11:26.770
You okay?

00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:28.060
Ribbit!

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:34.620
<i>How long has it been since Mom died?</i>

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:38.410
<i>Twenty-five years? No... Longer?</i>

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:41.470
<i>Letters?</i>

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:46.350
What are these? Dad's?

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:48.080
So many...

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:50.850
<b>Dear Tawara Udon, 

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:54.590
<i>This is... about Dad's udon?</i>

00:11:58.780 --> 00:11:59.620
Here.

00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:07.250
Thanks.

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:23.280
This used to be mine. You can wear it.

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:26.510
I'm not sure if the shoes will fit, though...

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:34.730
I know the feeling.

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:38.900
When I was little, for some reason, 
wearing a poncho always got me excited, too.

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:12.420
Can you tell the police officers

00:13:12.420 --> 00:13:14.580
your name when they ask?

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:18.150
You didn't learn how? You know...

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:21.740
"I'm Tawara Souta, 30 years old." Like that.

00:13:22.330 --> 00:13:23.530
Souta?

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:25.030
No, uh...

00:13:25.550 --> 00:13:27.160
Not <i>my</i> name...

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:29.200
Souta! Souta!

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:31.320
Souta! Souta!

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:31.620
Okay, okay.

00:13:31.320 --> 00:13:33.260
Souta! Souta!

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:33.820
Hello!

00:13:33.260 --> 00:13:34.160
Souta!

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:38.170
By any chance... Are you open?

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:40.000
Ah... Sorry.

00:13:40.350 --> 00:13:42.320
I hate to say it,

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:44.920
but the udon restaurant 
is no longer in business.

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:46.880
What?!

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:49.970
<b>Tawara Noodles</b>

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:48.040
Sorry!

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:49.650
I know the sign's still up...

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:52.010
Aww, man...

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:55.930
And here I thought Tawara Udon had come back...

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:56.650
Um...

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:59.400
Did you come by to eat it a lot?

00:13:59.640 --> 00:14:00.780
My dad's udon.

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:04.160
Yes! My workplace is right around the corner,

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:06.530
so I came 'round all the time.

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:08.210
Oh...

00:14:08.210 --> 00:14:09.080
Uh-huh!

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:13.330
Tawara-san's kamatama udon 
is one of my favorites.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:16.040
<b>Gurgle</b>

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:18.330
<i>Is that her stomach?!</i>

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:24.420
<b>Gorgle</b>

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:24.420
<b>Gurgle</b>

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:23.330
<i>Their tummies are grumbling in sync?!</i>

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:26.800
My lunch break's about to end!

00:14:27.370 --> 00:14:29.920
Sorry for interrupting you!

00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:30.680
It's fine...

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:36.060
If you ever reopen the restaurant, 
please let me know!

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:37.000
Huh?

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:44.250
Souta?

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:46.860
Souta!

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:52.850
Let's go.

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:08.050
Ribbit, ribbit!

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:11.010
Ribbit, ribbit!

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:11.010
Wait—

00:15:12.090 --> 00:15:13.580
Ouch!

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:26.740
Too many stairs...

00:15:26.740 --> 00:15:27.690
Hey!

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:29.700
Souta!

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:33.200
Come on, you shouldn't run 
off on your own like that.

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:35.260
Souta!

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:37.550
I thought this child was lost.

00:15:38.320 --> 00:15:40.230
I'm glad the father was here.

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:42.080
Oh, no, I'm not...

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:44.360
Do be careful.

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:47.850
If a child wanders around alone here,

00:15:48.540 --> 00:15:51.010
a tanuki could bewitch them.

00:15:51.270 --> 00:15:52.180
Oh...

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:56.510
There are stories of a shapeshifting 
tanuki appearing in these parts.

00:15:57.450 --> 00:16:01.380
They say that the tanuki 
takes on a human appearance,

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:04.790
and lives in the form of a 
child for years and years.

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:06.740
Really...

00:16:07.680 --> 00:16:08.430
Well...

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:11.190
Even for a tanuki,

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:13.890
I'm sure being alone for so very long

00:16:14.180 --> 00:16:16.250
must be quite a sad thing...

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:19.540
Ready to go?

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:31.920
Don't run off again, okay?

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:32.360
Souta! Souta! Souta!

00:16:29.950 --> 00:16:31.650
I know we're in the right area...

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:34.590
Yeah. That's weird.

00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:34.590
Souta! Souta!

00:16:33.040 --> 00:16:34.370
I'm here, I'm here.

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:36.970
Souta! Souta!

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:36.380
Oh, excuse me!

00:16:37.250 --> 00:16:39.940
There's supposed to be a restaurant

00:16:39.940 --> 00:16:41.880
called "Tawara Noodles" in this area...

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:44.980
Actually, that restaurant closed down.

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:47.400
What?! Are you sure?

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:50.000
But it's in the guidebook...

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:52.730
My family ran it, actually, so I am sure.

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:55.030
Huh? You're from the restaurant?

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:57.240
You don't make udon?

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:01.450
When I grow up,

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:03.830
I wanna be cool like Dad

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:06.130
and make handmade udon!

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:09.290
I don't, no.

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:12.440
You're not taking over the restaurant?

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:14.960
But if your family ran it, 
you <i>can</i> make udon, right?

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:15.750
No...

00:17:16.750 --> 00:17:19.380
You always stink like soup stock!

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:22.140
An udon restaurant? That's so lame!

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:23.840
We came all this way.

00:17:23.840 --> 00:17:26.860
I'd really love to eat the 
udon at Tawara Noodles!

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:27.400
Yeah!

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:29.800
No. There's no way I'm takin' over.

00:17:30.350 --> 00:17:31.860
I don't wanna run an udon restaurant.

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:34.420
I'm goin' to Tokyo.

00:17:35.690 --> 00:17:37.140
Do what ya want.

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:41.260
We'd be totally happy to eat your udon!

00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:42.290
Please?

00:17:42.980 --> 00:17:45.540
No, I really can't...

00:17:46.650 --> 00:17:50.920
<i>If it was that simple for me to take over...</i>

00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:57.850
Whoa! What's with this kid?

00:17:57.330 --> 00:17:58.640
H-Hey...

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:01.970
Ah! Don't! Don't hit there!

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:01.970
Hey!

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:03.630
Stop that!

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:05.910
<i>"Fluff"?</i>

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:08.890
<i>Ears?!</i>

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:10.690
<i>A tail?!</i>

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:12.610
Oh my God! Are you okay?!

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:12.610
Souta?

00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:14.880
<i>My instincts...</i>

00:18:17.550 --> 00:18:20.280
<i>are screaming, "Don't let them see this!"</i>

00:18:18.610 --> 00:18:19.960
Ah! Hey, wait!

00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:24.940
Was that... a tail?

00:18:24.940 --> 00:18:25.790
Huh?

00:18:29.310 --> 00:18:30.520
<i>What is this?</i>

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:32.930
<i>What the heck is going on?!</i>

00:19:03.230 --> 00:19:07.080
Am I dreaming this up?

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:09.420
Souta!

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:16.990
There are stories of a shapeshifting 
tanuki appearing in these parts.

00:19:17.890 --> 00:19:21.780
They say that the tanuki 
takes on a human appearance,

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:25.230
and lives in the form of a 
child for years and years.

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:31.660
Souta!

00:19:34.850 --> 00:19:37.780
What... are you?

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:09.950
<b>Gaogao-chan and</b>

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:09.950
<b>The Blue Sky</b>

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:15.960
<b>Episode 1</b>

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:15.960
<b>"Gaogao-chan and the Blue Planet"</b>

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:13.670
<i>The Tale of Gaogao-chan</i>

00:21:13.670 --> 00:21:15.960
<i>and the Blue Planet!</i>

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:20.320
<i>Far away on the edge of space, in Galazy M87,</i>

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:25.030
<i>lived the most fearsome alien in the universe.</i>

00:21:25.390 --> 00:21:26.900
<i>Gao...</i>

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:27.730
<i>Gao...</i>

00:21:28.740 --> 00:21:30.840
<i>Gao!</i>

00:21:31.550 --> 00:21:33.190
<i>I sure am bright,</i>

00:21:33.190 --> 00:21:34.140
<i>because I'm the sun!</i>

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:38.260
<i>And this is an automobile repair shop</i>

00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:40.180
<i>somewhere on Earth.</i>

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:42.910
<i>The kind mechanics, Mimi and Momo,</i>

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:45.050
<i>are hard at work today.</i>

00:21:45.050 --> 00:21:48.410
<i>We're not getting any customers at all!</i>

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:50.350
<i>It's just how it is, Mimi.</i>

00:21:50.350 --> 00:21:53.790
<i>After all, none of our 
neighborhood friends use cars!</i>

00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:56.100
<i>I'm sorry, Momo-chan.</i>

00:21:56.100 --> 00:21:58.500
<i>If only I were a little braver,</i>

00:21:58.500 --> 00:22:00.540
<i>I could ride in a car...</i>

00:22:01.240 --> 00:22:03.150
<i>It's okay, Cat.</i>

00:22:03.150 --> 00:22:05.660
<i>Here, have some rice balls and cheer up!</i>

00:22:05.970 --> 00:22:09.470
<i>Argh! If only there'd be an accident nearby!</i>

00:22:09.470 --> 00:22:11.610
<i>Then we could fix the car!</i>

00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:14.450
<i>Don't say that, now—</i>

00:22:20.910 --> 00:22:23.890
<i>I am the most fearsome 
alien in the universe,</i>

00:22:24.220 --> 00:22:26.340
<i>Ipalnemoani Gaogao.</i>

00:22:26.730 --> 00:22:29.370
<i>I have come to invade your Earth.</i>

00:22:31.510 --> 00:22:32.340
<i>Huh?</i>

00:22:32.340 --> 00:22:33.370
<i>Huh?</i>

00:22:34.120 --> 00:22:35.370
